  "worked_solution": "Let $\\delta >0.$ A *neighborhood* of a point ${x}_{0}$ is the set of points whose distance from ${x}_{0}$ is less than $\\delta .$\n\n$$\n{x:|x-{x}_{0}|<\\delta }\n$$\n\nIn two-dimensional space, a neighborhood of ${x}_{0}$ is the open disc $|x-{x}_{0}|<\\delta ,$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041362/assets/50a6c72e169f3104eb0b9958673cc6644f770e6bcc3ebf23360eb20189325a28.png)\n\nFurthermore, we have the following definitions:\n\n- A point ${x}_{0}$ is an *interior point* of a set $S$ if $S$ contains *some* neighborhood of ${x}_{0}.$ The set of all interior points of $S$ is called the *interior* of $S.$\n\n- A point ${x}_{0}$ is a *boundary point* of a set $S$ if *every* neighborhood of ${x}_{0}$ contains points that are in $S$ and points that are not in $S.$ \nThe set of all boundary points of $S$ is called the *boundary* of $S.$\n\nNow, the set $A$ consists of all points that lie on or to the left of the line $x=1.$ A sketch of this region is shown below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041362/assets/119fbce04df572e5b1c083432d0183da1cc04add5e4ad56ac7704af3cf8ee024.png)\n\nLet's add the points $P(1,2)$ and $Q(2,-2)$ and some neighborhoods of these points to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041362/assets/7dc96640505a272ec9701a9d155f7ed2809e6f6df29ac5327af6b2b2324fa162.png)\n\nLet's examine the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, $Q$ is not an interior point of $A$ since any neighborhood of $Q$ contains at least one point *outside* the set.\n\n- Statement II is true. The coordinates of $P(1,2)$ satisfy the equation $x=1.$ Hence, $P$ lies in the set $\u2202A,$ the boundary of $A.$\n\n- Statement III is true. The coordinates of $P(1,2)$ satisfy the inequality $x\\le 1.$ Hence, $P$ lies in the set $A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 'II and III only.'",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
